numeric : Check whether all characters are numeric.\n3640 |     Series.str.isalnum : Check whether all characters are alphanumeric.\n3641 |     Series.str.isdigit : Check whether all characters are digits.\n3642 |     Series.str.isdecimal : Check whether all characters are decimal.\n3643 |     Series.str.isspace : Check whether all characters are whitespace.\n3644 |     Series.str.islower : Check whether all characters are lowercase.\n3645 |     Series.str.istitle : Check whether all characters are titlecase.\n3646 | \n3647 |     Examples\n3648 |     --------\n3649 | \n3650 |     >>> s5 = pd.Series(['leopard', 'Golden Eagle', 'SNAKE', ''])\n3651 |     >>> s5.str.isupper()\n3652 |     0    False\n3653 |     1    False\n3654 |     2     True\n3655 |     3    False\n3656 |     dtype: bool\n3657 |     \"\"\"\n3658 |     _shared_docs[\"istitle\"] = \"\"\"\n3659 |     See Also\n3660 |     --------\n3661 |     Series.str.isalpha : Check whether all characters are alphabetic.\n3662 |     Series.str.isnumeric : Check whether all characters are numeric.\n3663 |     Series.str.isalnum : Check whether all characters are alphanumeric.\n3664 |     Series.str.isdigit : Check whether all characters are digits.\n3665 |     Series.str.isdecimal : Check whether all characters are decimal.\n3666 |     Series.str.isspace : Check whether all characters are whitespace.\n3667 |     Series.str.islower : Check whether all characters are lowercase.\n3668 |     Series.str.isupper : Check whether all characters are uppercase.\n3669 | \n3670 |     Examples\n3671 |     ------------\n3672 |     The ``s5.str.istitle`` method checks for whether all words are in title\n3673 |     case (whether only the first letter of each word is capitalized). Words are\n3674 |     assumed to be as any sequence of non-numeric characters separated by\n3675 |     whitespace characters.\n3676 | \n3677 |     >>> s5 = pd.Series(['leopard', 'Golden Eagle', 'SNAKE', ''])\n3678 |     >>> s5.str.istitle()\n3679 |     0    Fa